---
description: Build full pages and entire sites in one uninterrupted batch from Figma. Always use grey placeholder boxes for images.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Page build protocol — batch mode

**Never pause between sections for approval. Build the complete page in one shot.**

---

## Phase A — Full page scan (zero code yet)

1. Call Figma MCP on the target page frame and get **ALL direct children at once**.
   Do not request sections one by one. One call, full list.
2. Take a full-scroll screenshot of the page for visual reference.
3. Write a **SECTION MAP** before touching any file — list every section:

   ```
   Section 1 · [Figma frame name] · node [id] → P-01 Hero2 (variant=overlay)
   Section 2 · [Figma frame name] · node [id] → P-18 HowAgingWorks
   Section 3 · [Figma frame name] · node [id] → ⚠️  NO MATCH — new widget needed
   Section 4 · [Figma frame name] · node [id] → P-19 EverythingPeaks
   ```

   Match against `src/registry/components.json` using `figmaNames` and `shape`.
   Flag every unmatched section ⚠️ **before writing any code**.

---

## Phase B — Gap handling (new widgets only)

For every ⚠️ flagged section:

1. Screenshot that section in Figma for close inspection.
2. Build `src/components/widgets/[NewName].astro` to match Figma exactly.
   - Use brand tokens from `src/brand.ts` — never hardcode hex.
   - Use existing atoms (`Button`, `Heading`, `Text`, `Card`, …) — never duplicate them.
3. Register the new widget in `src/registry/components.json`:
   ```json
   {
     "id": "P-XX",
     "name": "Descriptive Name",
     "figmaNames": ["Figma Frame Name", "Figma node id"],
     "shape": "one-line description of the layout shape",
     "component": "NewName",
     "import": "~/components/widgets/NewName.astro",
     "props": { "…": "…" },
     "notes": "Figma node [id]. …"
   }
   ```
4. Mark it ✅ in the section map and **immediately continue** — do not wait for approval.

All gap widgets must be resolved **before** the page file is started.

---

## Phase C — Compose the full page (one shot)

Write `src/pages/[route]/index.astro` completely in a **single edit**:

### Structure

```astro
---
// 1. Framework + widget imports
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Hero2 from '~/components/widgets/Hero2.astro';
// …all widgets listed in section map

// 2. Config / data imports
import { site } from '~/config/site';
import { PRIMARY_CTA_LABEL, PRIMARY_CTA_HREF } from '~/config/cta';

// 3. Inline data (SVGs, arrays, objects) — all data at the top, never inline in JSX
const items = [ … ];

// 4. Metadata
const metadata = { title: '…', description: '…' };
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <!-- widgets composed top-to-bottom matching section map -->
</Layout>
```

### Rules during composition

- **One widget per section** — never paste raw markup into the page file.
- **Data before layout** — define all arrays, SVGs, and objects in the frontmatter block.
- **Props inline** — pass data as widget props; keep page file readable.
- Follow the `tokens` rule: use `text-heading`, `bg-section-grey`, `text-accent`, etc. No hex.

---

## Image placeholders — ALWAYS

Every place Figma shows a photo, illustration, chart, or background image:

```astro
<!-- TODO: replace with <Image> when asset is ready -->
<div
  class="w-full rounded-[32px] bg-section-grey"
  style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;"
  aria-hidden="true"
/>
```

- Read the exact aspect ratio from the Figma frame (e.g. `507 / 657`, `1200 / 630`).
- Match `rounded-*` to the Figma corner radius.
- Use `bg-section-grey` always — never a real image, never a Figma MCP localhost URL.
- This applies to **every** image slot, including hero backgrounds, split images, card covers, and OG thumbnails.
- Do not skip this for "obvious" images. Every image = grey box until the asset pass.

---

## Multi-page site builds (20–30 pages)

When building an entire site from Figma:

1. **List all pages** and their Figma node IDs upfront in a plan comment.
2. Run Phase A → B → C for **page 1**, then **immediately continue to page 2** without pausing.
3. Reuse widgets built in Phase B — do not rebuild the same pattern for a later page.
4. Only stop between pages if a structural decision affects the design system or atoms
   (e.g. a new atom needed in `src/components/ui/`). Fix it, then resume.
5. **Run `npm run build` once** after all pages are complete. Fix all errors together.
   Do not build after each individual page.

---

## Do not

- Stop after a section and say "shall I continue?" or "here is section 1, let me know if you want me to proceed"
- Start writing a page file before the full section map is done
- Start Phase C before all ⚠️ gaps are resolved
- Create a new widget without adding it to `src/registry/components.json`
- Import or embed real image files from any source during a page build
- Use Figma MCP localhost image URLs anywhere in production code
- Hardcode hex colours (`#1B2A32`, `#E5DDCF`, …) in widgets or pages
- Fork a section per route (`HomeFAQ.astro`, `AboutHero.astro`, `ServicesCTA.astro`)
- Run `npm run build` after every page on a multi-page build
